  "id": "Compound::DB01336 - Gene::1134",
  "verbalization": "Metocurine is likely to interact with Chrna1 through a series of molecular and functional pathways. The evidence suggests that Metocurine binds to Chrnb1, a subunit of the acetylcholine receptor, which is involved in the regulation of ion channels. This binding may modulate the activity of the acetylcholine-activated cation-selective channel, which is ultimately associated with Chrna1. The integration of these pathways implies that Metocurine exerts its effects by influencing the function of the acetylcholine receptor complex, thereby potentially affecting the activity of Chrna1. The overlapping roles of Chrnb1 in different pathways highlight the importance of this subunit in mediating the effects of Metocurine on ion channel activity, suggesting a direct or indirect relationship between the drug and the receptor.",
